                <pb facs="0636" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                                1919—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3214. Department’s 3145, September 16, 5 p.m., and No. 3151 of September 16, 8
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>American Legation, Brussels, reports that Supreme Economic Council voted,
                    September 21, to uphold decision of Allied Maritime Transport Executive,
                    withdrawing exemption of tank steamers granted by Brussels agreement, refusing
                    present use of D.A.P.G. tankers for commercial voyages, and directing tankers be
                    immediately sent to Firth of Forth for allocation.</p>
                <p>Department urges every effort be made, for reasons set forth in previous
                    instructions, to have Supreme Council overrule decision of Supreme Economic
                    Council, and allow present utilization of tank steamers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
